cture","content":"**`ButtonGroup`** — a cluster of related actions, typically inside a `Footer` (an end-aligned, wrapping row with `role=\"group\"`)."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-14","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"Each container works in two modes:"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-15","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"**Standalone** — with no parent context it renders with its own structural defaults and looks the same everywhere."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-16","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"**Adopted** — placed inside a parent that provides its context (`ContentContext`, `HeaderContext`, `FooterContext`, `ButtonGroupContext`), it picks up that parent's styling and spacing automatically. Merge precedence is defaults \\< parent context \\< consumer props (`className` concatenates, handlers chain), via React Aria's `useContextProps`."},"1220":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-17","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#hybrid-styling","content":"A parent adopts them by providing the contexts around its children:"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-18","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#default","content":"The shared structural containers composed together into a card-like layout. Each is a\nplain semantic region here; inside a parent that provides their contexts (e.g. `Modal`)\nthey adopt that parent's spacing automatically."},"1222":{"id":"/docs/components/structure-19","page_id":"/docs/components/structure","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/structure#props","content":"`Content`, `Header`, `Footer`, and `ButtonGroup` ea